From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eddy Flores <eddyflores100@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: apply reviewer feedback — version ~> v2 and trim comment

Applies the two changes requested by @SakshhamTheCoder:
1. Use `version: '~> v2'` instead of `version: v2`
2. Trim the comment to one line

Closes #35. Updates #48.

---
 .github/workflows/release.yml | 8 ++------
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/release.yml b/.github/workflows/release.yml
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/release.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/release.yml
@@ -40,12 +40,8 @@ jobs:
       - name: Run GoReleaser
         uses: goreleaser/goreleaser-action@v6
         with:
-          # Pin to v2 to avoid breaking changes from latest (v3 introduced
-          # breaking changes in the config format that broke our releases).
-          # See: https://github.com/goreleaser/goreleaser-action/releases/tag/v3.0.0
-          # Track: issue #35
-          version: v2
+          # Pin to v2 to avoid breaking changes from latest.
+          version: '~> v2'
           distribution: goreleaser
           args: release --clean
         env:
-- 
2.39.3
